VeridianOS: KSortFilterProxyModel: port invalidateFilter() to endFilterChange()

GCC reported 'void QSortFilterProxyModel::invalidateFilter()' is deprecated:
Use begin/endFilterChange() instead [-Wdeprecated-declarations] in
src/qml/ksortfilterproxymodel.cpp:311.

KSortFilterProxyModel::invalidateFilter() is a QML-invokable slot that
callers use after they have changed what their filter callbacks depend on,
so there is no "before" point at which to call beginFilterChange(). In Qt,
the deprecated QSortFilterProxyModel::invalidateFilter() is
filter_changed(Rows | Columns), which is exactly
endFilterChange(Direction::Both); the slot now calls that. No behaviour
change. Requires Qt >= 6.10 (endFilterChange()).

diff -ru a/src/qml/ksortfilterproxymodel.cpp b/src/qml/ksortfilterproxymodel.cpp
--- a/src/qml/ksortfilterproxymodel.cpp	2026-10-08 17:16:38.781249165 -0400
+++ b/src/qml/ksortfilterproxymodel.cpp	2026-10-08 17:16:38.817514110 -0400
@@ -308,7 +308,8 @@
 
 void KSortFilterProxyModel::invalidateFilter()
 {
-    QSortFilterProxyModel::invalidateFilter();
+    // Called after the filter parameters changed: refilter rows and columns.
+    endFilterChange(QSortFilterProxyModel::Direction::Both);
 }
 
 #include "moc_ksortfilterproxymodel.cpp"
